{{Term/Store|Horseback Archery||Series, BotW}}, also known as the '''Horseback Archery Challenge''',<ref>{{Cite|Hey, newcomer, you have a fine horse! I don't know where you stole it from, but... OK, how about this {{Color OoT3D|Red|horseback archery challenge}}?|Gerudo|OoT3D}}</ref>{{Exp Game|OoT}} is a recurring [[Mini-Game]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite Guide|BotW Piggyback|page= 332}}</ref> Horseback Archery goes unnamed in {{MM}}.

==Location and Rules==
==={{OoT|-}}===
{{Main|Horseback Archery Range}}
A Horseback Archery Minigame takes place at the [[Horseback Archery Range]] at the rear of [[Gerudo's Fortress]] and requires a [[Gerudo Token]] in order to play. Each attempt costs 20 [[Rupee]]s. [[Link]] must mount [[Epona]] and fire up to 20 [[Arrow]]s at a series of targets while she gallops around the range; more accurate hits gain him more points. Scoring 1,000 points or more wins Link a [[Piece of Heart]], and scoring 1,500 or more on a later attempt wins him an upgraded [[Quiver]].

==={{MM|-}}===
In order to prevent the [[Ghost (Majora's Mask)|Ghosts]] from stealing the [[Cow]]s from [[Romani Ranch]],<ref>{{Cite|Romani was practicing... For tonight... Tonight...|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color MM3D|Red|They}} are coming...|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|They... They come at night...every year when the carnival approaches... They come riding in a bright, shining ball. A whole lot of them come down... And then... They come to the barn...|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|My older sister won't believe me... But Romani must protect the cows!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref> [[Romani]] appoints Link as her assistant. If Link agrees to help her, she explains her strategy and tasks Link with riding the Ranch's Horse, [[Epona]], to destroy the 10 Ghost-shaped [[Balloon]]s that she places across the Ranch in under 2 minutes.<ref>{{Cite|Hey, Grasshopper, I'm recruiting for an assistant right now! You're a boy--won't you try?|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color MM3D|Green|[Yes]}} Great! Now that's the spirit, Grasshopper! OK then, I'm going straight into my strategy!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|They'll appear all over the ranch... They'll aim for the barn and approach it slowly, so hit them with {{Color MM3D|Red|arrows}} so they can't get in! You got that? And you mustn't {{Color MM3D|Red|leave}} the ranch!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Grasshopper! Let's practice right away!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|There are {{Color MM3D|Red|10}} ghost-shaped {{Color MM3D|Red|balloons}} in the ranch, so hurry and burst them all. If you take more than {{Color MM3D|Red|2 minutes}}, you're out.|Romani|MM3D}}</ref>

During the Mini-Game, red-colored dots will appear on the [[Map Screen]], indicating the positions of the remaining Balloons. Link is unable to dismount Epona during the Mini-Game. Likewise, a [[Gate]] will be set up at the entrance to Romani Ranch to prevent Link from escaping. If Link speaks to Romani during the Mini-Game, she will laugh and remark on how confident he is.<ref>{{Cite|Confident, aren't you?|Romani|MM3D}}</ref>

Upon first completing the Mini-Game within the time limit, Romani will tell Link that he and Epona work perfectly together.<ref>{{Cite|OK! You're done!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You two work perfectly together!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref> She then decides to teach Link "[[Epona's Song]]" so that he can call upon the Horse when he needs.<ref>{{Cite|I'll teach Romani's horse-calling song to you, Grasshopper. Now you two keep getting along, and go practice some more!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref>{{Note|If Link does not beat the current record but completes the practice in under 2 minutes, Romani will simply tell him that he did great.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color MM3D|Red|XX:XX.XX}}! That's great.|Romani|MM3D}}</ref> If Link beats Romani's record of 1 minute,<ref>{{Cite|The current record is {{Color MM3D|Red|01:00.00}}. Are you ready?|Romani|MM3D}}</ref> she will congratulate him instead.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color MM3D|Red|XX:XX.XX}}?!? Amazing! It's a new record!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref> Additionally, if Link fails to complete the practice in the time limit, she will dismiss the result as a consequence of his inexperience.<ref>{{Cite|OK! Time's up!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Too bad. Well, that's how it goes at first, Grasshopper.|Romani|MM3D}}</ref>}} Afterwards, Romani will caution Link that unlike the practice Balloons, the real Ghosts will keep appearing even after being destroyed and that they must hold out until sunrise at 5:00 AM.<ref>{{Cite|When your arrows hit these, they burst into nothing, but the real ones will keep popping up! If they get in the barn, we lose! They run away at first {{Color MM3D|Red|light}} of the {{Color MM3D|Red|sun}}, so we'll have to keep fending them off until then!|Romani|MM3D}}</ref>

The Horseback Archery Mini-Game can be attempted multiple times during a cycle, although Link will not receive any additional prizes for practicing. It can only be attempted on the [[First Day]] as the Ghosts will either abduct Romani if Link fails to fend them off, or there will be no need with the threat of invasion gone on subsequent days.

==={{BotW|-}}===
The Horseback Archery [[Mini-Game]] is operated by [[Jini]] at the [[Mounted Archery Camp]]. When [[Link]] first approaches him, he asks how confident he is in his ability to fight on horseback.<ref>{{Cite|Hello there, young man. I can tell just by looking that you're a trained warrior. But tell me this: How confident are you in your ability to fight on horseback?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link is not confident, Jini expresses concern and asks if he would like to run some drills.<ref>{{Cite|Hm... I don't like the sound of that. The monsters out this way are strong critters. You're sure you don't want to {{Color BotW|Red|drill}} with me some?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link is confident, Jini asks if he is willing to prove it.<ref>{{Cite|Yeah? You got the skills to back that confidence up? Nothing's more dangerous than a man who thinks he can handle the worst, only to fall apart when the time comes. What do you think? Are you confident enough to {{Color BotW|Red|prove you got the right stuff}}?|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

Link can ask Jini how the drills work. Jini explains that Horseback Archery was invented somewhere in the east,<ref>{{Cite|Ever heard of {{Color BotW|Red|horseback archery}}? They invented it way out east somewhere.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> and it requires a lot of coordination.<ref>{{Cite|It takes a lot of coordination to shoot targets with a bow and arrow from the back of a galloping horse.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He claims his drill will be a good way to practice fighting mounted [[Enemies in Breath of the Wild|monsters]].<ref>{{Cite|I expect you'll run into mounted varmints now and again, so this'll be a good way to get some practice in.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

If Link is not riding a [[Horse]], Jini will notice.<ref>{{Cite|Now...for a young man interested in horseback archery, you seem to be in want of a horse. That's no way to {{Color BotW|Red|drill}}.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He instructs Link to retrieve one of his Horses from [[Highland Stable]] nearby and to come back riding it.<ref>{{Cite|Head down that path there, and you ought to come across a {{Color BotW|Red|stable}}. Fetch your steed from them if you got one. Get a horse, mount up, then come talk to me {{Color BotW|Red|when you're riding high in the saddle.}}|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

When Link agrees to run a drill, Jini reminds him that he can not do so without a [[Bow]] and [[Arrow]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Can't drill without a {{Color BotW|Red|bow and arrows}}. I'd think that's just common sense.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He offers to sell Arrows and do other kinds of business with Link.<ref>{{Cite|If you need some, I can sell you a few of mine. Or I'm open for any sort of business! What do you say?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He encourages Link to take his time as he browses his wares.<ref>{{Cite|I have an impressive collection here! Take your time!|Jini|BotW}}</ref> However, if Link denies him, Jini says that they will see how well he does on the field with his Horse.<ref>{{Cite|Suit yourself. We'll see how well you and your horse act as a team on the field.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

The price to run a drill is 20 [[Rupee]]s,<ref>{{Cite|Now...I'm loath to ask, but would you mind forking over {{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}} to cover some of my costs?|Jini|BotW}}|</ref> though Jini guarantees they are worth twice as much.<ref>{{Cite|Much obliged, young man. I guarantee my {{Color BotW|Red|drills}} are worth twice what you pay.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link refuses to pay, Jini explains that while he is happy to provide his Horseback Archery drills, he has needs to meet.<ref>{{Cite|This here's a service I'm happy to provide, but I can't do it for free. Don't judge a man for his needs.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

The goal of the Mini-Game is to pop as many of the [[Balloon]]s floating in the [[Parache Plains]].<ref>{{Cite|I'll explain a bit before we get started. You see the {{Color BotW|Red|targets}} floating out there? I'll judge your skill by {{Color BotW|Red|how many of 'em you pop with your arrows}}.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> Jini tells Link not to worry about time, as he will let him know when it is up.<ref>{{Cite|Don't you worry about when time's up. I'll let you know.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> In addition, he informs Link that he is not allowed to dismount his Horse during the drill.<ref>{{Cite|Suppose this goes without saying but you get off your horse, and we're done here. No way to practice shooting from horseback when you're standing around on foot, after all.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He promises Link some [[Horse Gear]] if he can break more than 20 Balloons.<ref>{{Cite|Tell you what... You break {{Color BotW|Red|more than 20}} targets, and I'll hand over my {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}}|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

Link can speak to Jini during the Mini-Game.<ref>{{Cite|Hm? What's the matter?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link says it is nothing, Jini says no one likes a quitter and he should continue with the drill.<ref>{{Cite|Good. No one likes a quitter. There's still time, so ride hard and shoot straight. Until then, ride hard and shoot straight.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> However, if Link asks to forfeit the run, Jini tells him he will not get his Rupees back and asks if he still wants to quit.<ref>{{Cite|That's fair. Course, you won't get your money back, if that's what you're after. Still planning to quit?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> When Link chooses to quit, Jini figures that he must have his reasons and encourages him to come again.<ref>{{Cite|I suppose you have your reasons. Hope to see you again someday.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

Once time runs out, Jini calls Link back to the Mounted Archery Camp.<ref>{{Cite|Hold it! Head on back here.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link hit less than 11 Balloons, he suggests trying to shoot while the Horse is trotting instead of galloping.<ref>{{Cite|Hm... You only hit {{Color BotW|Red|[X]}}... Nothing to write home about. Might want to shoot from {{Color BotW|Red|a trot}} some more before you jump straight into firing at a gallop.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> There is no reward. Between 12 and 19 Balloons, Jini is not convinced of Link's skill and reminds him to keep his eye on the targets.<ref>{{Cite|Hm... Well, you hit {{Color BotW|Red|[X]}}... Not bad, but I'm not rightly convinced you're ready to raise the stakes. Hitting your mark at a gallop is no small potatoes. Make sure to {{Color BotW|Red|keep your eye}} on the target.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> As a reward, he gives Link 15 Arrows.<ref>{{Cite|Here's a reward for seeing it through. Keep drilling and you'll get it.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> When Link pops between 20 and 22 Balloons, Jini says he has the potential to be among the best archers and gives him the [[Knight's Bridle]].<ref>{{Cite|Hm...{{Color BotW|Red|[X] targets}}... You've got some fire in you, young man. The best archers say {{Color BotW|Red|targets seem to freeze when they concentrate on them}}. I think you could reach that level too. Here's a gift to help you on your travels. Hope you find a good use for it.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link already has the Knight's Bridle, Jini will instead give him 10 [[Bomb Arrow]]s.}} Finally, if Link hits between 23 and 25 targets, Jini will say he has not seen someone so young with such talent in a long time.<ref>{{Cite|Hm...{{Color BotW|Red|[X] targets}}... It's been a dog's age since I've seen such talent in someone so young.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He does not believe that Link is actually over 100 years old and gives him the [[Knight's Saddle]], as he no longer needs it.<ref>{{Cite|What do you mean you're not that young? Over 100 years old? Go ahead, pull the other one. Anyway, this gift is my thanks for putting on a good show. I'm past needing it, and I think you should have it.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link already has the Knight's Saddle, Jini will instead give him 20 Bomb Arrows.}}

After each drill Link runs, Jini asks if he wants to go again.<ref>{{Cite|Well? You want to {{Color BotW|Red|drill}} some more?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link refuses, Jini reminds him not to be a stranger and to come back.<ref>{{Cite|[I'm in a hurry...] Don't be a stranger, young man. I'll be waiting here for you, come wind or storm.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> If Link agrees, Jini says he made the right call and asks for 20 more Rupees.<ref>{{Cite|Sounds like the right call to me. The price hasn't gone down any—{{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}}, same as ever. That fine with you?|Jini|BotW}}</ref> Once Link has paid, he goes to fix the targets that were destroyed in the previous run.<ref>{{Cite|I'll go fix up the targets. Shouldn't be long.|Jini|BotW}}</ref> He is able to run a drill once they are fixed.<ref>{{Cite|All done now. Let's get drilling again.|Jini|BotW}}</ref>

